id: pm-slack-destination-migration-plans
title: Preview and review destination changes for pending Slack events
description: "Preview explicit alias-to-alias route transitions on the durable Slack outbox. The outbox remains the delivery engine; route configuration changes are separate from reliability, notification disclosure and standup digest policies."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: outbox,routing,slack
created_at: "2026-10-28T20:32:57.205Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-29T00:07:56.718Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: No event silently targets both old and new destinations; already uncertain sends retain uncertainty; replay creates no duplicate queue entries; preview posts nothing; queued use of the new route requires a reviewed binding revision.
comments[18]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-28T20:33:39.405Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked on 2026-10-28: pm-slack main 911d78a owns SQLite delivery, history recovery, coalescing and route explanations; no open destination-migration PR or issue exists. CLI public SDK declarations expose tracker transactions, status registries, history and complete reads, but no Slack route migration API. Standup main f1d1187 builds reports; observer main 7aba36e queues PM evidence notes; ops has no Slack routing transition. This feature reuses the durable outbox and its delivery proof, not another delivery engine or disclosure policy. Planned design: explicit aliases bind to credential-free existing configured routes; monotonic binding revision and exact queue-plan revision require review; preview uses the same evaluator as atomic apply; uncertainty and receipt identities survive. Plans cover only currently pending, proven-unsent owned receipts. Tracker records are observed through SDK complete/history reads and never rewritten."
  "2026-10-28T20:41:06.665Z",codex-agent,"Implemented typed migrateSlackDestinations and offline slack migrate CLI. Alias binding writes are revision-fenced; preview uses SQLite read-only with byte-equality proof; atomic apply reuses the same evaluator and triggers fence old/new drainers plus ABA edits. Replays retain one immutable delivery identity and re-read every applied target. Uncertain and unfinished attempts remain on the original route, including force-retired live senders. Found and fixed coalesced-drain stale-route race by revalidating destination inside claim. First focused regressions passed 7/7; typecheck and docstring gate passed. Building 500-sequence model and exhaustive statement-boundary concurrency/crash tests next."
  "2026-10-28T20:52:04.707Z",codex-agent,"Public read-only tracker validation at main 911d78a: 94 items and verified streams, 849 history entries, 240 lifecycle events and unique queue entries. Reviewed revision 2 moved 237 events and retained 3 uncertain sends, including a pending retry. Replay moved zero; duplicate entries and remote posts zero. Preview database bytes, full SDK-read native state and all source tracker bytes unchanged. Focused suite passed 84 tests with migration module 100 percent lines, branches and functions, including 500 seeded sequences and exhaustive peer/interruption boundaries. Typecheck, test typecheck and docstring gate passed. npm/Bun full release checks remain assigned to CI; packed host-shape acceptance is in progress."
  "2026-10-28T20:58:55.207Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof in a disposable source copy: reverting route reassignment, the queue revision guard, uncertainty retention, original-intent replay acceptance or coalesced claim destination revalidation independently made its focused regression fail. Restored functions passed all four selected regression scenarios. Native Bun SDK/CLI acceptance passed including migration and old-input replay. The captured package passed five real host installation shapes (project local, npm global, Bun global, npx and bunx) with one move, one receipt and zero posts each; final artifact is being recaptured after the last output-safety test. A transient CLI fixture omitted a required routing override; corrected it and the isolated CLI test passed. Linked tests are rerunning with a 300-second bound. Local health is blocked only by pre-existing pm-github host 2026.10.28 versus pinned host 2026.10.24 skew, plus an inherited advisory already tracked separately; history remains append-only."
  "2026-10-28T21:01:46.690Z",codex-agent,"Final linked runner passed 3 of 3 commands: the 89-test migration regression suite (500 seeded random sequences, 4000 generated operations plus 500 fresh preview/apply comparisons), typecheck and docstring gate. The runner retains its inherited test-result tracking-disabled policy; evidence is recorded in this comment instead of changing policy. Five packed host shapes and native Bun acceptance passed. Read-only public validation remains 94 items, 849 entries, 240 events, 237 moves, 3 retained uncertain and zero duplicates/posts. Output-safety tests cover nonfinite JSON, deep payloads, bounds, invalid counters and isolated foreign records. Full unchanged npm/Bun release gates and source coverage are required on the pushed head in CI; final run URLs and counts will be attached to the PR. No merge, release or upstream repository write is authorized."
  "2026-10-28T21:07:03.587Z",codex-agent,"Final extreme-value review found one additional foreign-record boundary: SQLite can throw before row validation when a persisted per-event integer exceeds the JavaScript safe range, and one malformed proof row must not block healthy events. Adding lossless text reads for per-event counters plus per-row SDK proof fallback, and treating unsafe replay target revisions as isolated foreign receipts. This does not change the migration or delivery identity contract. Fresh exact-head CI will supersede the initial queued run."
  "2026-10-28T21:11:13.050Z",codex-agent,"Oversized native SQLite revision/proof regression passed, including healthy-event progress and isolated foreign replay receipts. Behavioral revert to the initial implementation failed that regression; restoring the fix passed. Latest linked run passed 3/3 commands with 90/90 migration tests, typecheck and docstring. Additional targeted foreign/JSON cases passed after reusing the outbox producer validator. Public validation was rerun unchanged: 94 items, 849 verified entries, 240 events, 237 moved, 3 uncertain, zero duplicate entries/posts. Initial CI run 40768782897 remains queued and is not gate evidence; a fresh exact-head run is required after this correction. Reviewer services skipped or exhausted quota, so no automated review approval is claimed."
  "2026-10-28T21:27:09.190Z",codex-agent,"Recorded a separate existing inspection limitation as pm-slack-outbox-foreign-native-counters: a synthetic non-git reproduction with one event and one oversized foreign proof counter makes SlackOutbox.status throw RangeError. Migration itself now skips that record and preserves healthy progress; public-data and current-plan acceptance remain met. This follow-up concerns general outbox inspection, not another route migration or delivery engine. Current code head d972dd7 passed both Node 26 release gates (885 tests each, six source files at 100 percent lines/branches/functions) and native Bun acceptance; Node 22 is running. The final tracker-evidence commit requires a fresh exact-head CI run."
  "2026-10-28T21:42:57.687Z",codex-agent,"Final producer/preview agreement audit found two concrete boundary cases in the new feature: preview did not preflight revision-capacity exhaustion, and adding a target channel could emit a payload above the documented size cap that a later preview would reject. Moving capacity and mapped-payload validation into the shared evaluator, counting payloads in UTF-8 bytes, and adding exact-boundary regressions before the final gate. Current source and tracker heads passed their release gates; those results do not certify this correction."
  "2026-10-28T21:49:22.752Z",codex-agent,"Shared planning now preflights global revision capacity and isolates exhausted per-event revisions. Target payloads are mapped and UTF-8 size-validated by the same evaluator before either preview or apply; apply uses those exact produced bytes. Exact 1 MiB payloads remain valid through reverse migration and SDK read-back, while channel growth and multibyte oversize records remain unchanged. Linked checks passed 3/3, including 92/92 tests and all 500 random sequences. Two additional independent behavioral reverts failed the capacity and payload regressions; restored code passed. Typecheck, test typecheck and docstring passed. No new feature edits are planned beyond required CI fixes; final build, package and CI evidence will bind this correction."
  "2026-10-28T22:22:47.450Z",codex-agent,"Re-review round 1 confirmed: the general violated rule is that scheduling authorization, uncertainty holds and transport identity must use one destination re-read inside the writer fence. Plain drains checked a stale candidate destination, while only coalesced claims validated their planned destination. Class audit found exactly two claim callers, plain and coalesced, both shared by SDK/CLI consumers. Plan: put expected-destination and held-destination checks in the shared claim transaction for every caller, send and record holds using the claimed destination, and cover every migration timing boundary plus SDK/CLI JSON/TOON and packed npm/Bun consumers. Worktree is clean and 4 commits ahead with zero behind origin/main; no merge is required. GitHub reviews and the supplied local review contain no additional actionable non-blocking finding."
  "2026-10-28T22:41:31.031Z",codex-agent,"Round 1 implementation: both claim callers now pass an expected destination and the same-drain hold set into the shared writer-fenced claim. It re-reads complete membership, refuses changed or held destinations before any attempt, and both send paths account against the claimed destination. Original implementation reproduced two B sends after the first became ambiguous; the new regression failed before the fix. Focused routing suite passed 81/81, including all executed SQL drain boundaries, independent SQLite peer migrations and real HTTP reset tests for both CLI commands with SDK/JSON/TOON agreement. Existing tests were retained. Native Bun acceptance passed the three new hold scenarios. Full-gate runner now caps test workers at two without changing thresholds."
  "2026-10-28T22:45:34.526Z",codex-agent,"Round 1 behavioral revert proof in disposable source copies: restoring the previous coherent drain/claim class reproduces the double B send; removing only expected-destination validation fails both stale-candidate drain tests; removing only the shared held-destination validation fails plain, urgent-coalesced and routine-coalesced ambiguity regressions. Every failure was an assertion about behavior, not a compile or import failure. Restored class passed all five selected regressions. The new focused suite passed 81/81 and preserves the earlier 500-sequence model and all existing tests. Both full release gates will now run serially with an enforced maximum of two test workers, a clean home and no inherited credentials."
  "2026-10-28T23:20:24.405Z",codex-agent,"Re-review validation: npm run release:check passed 968/968 tests with zero failures and 100% lines, branches and functions for all six runtime sources; unchanged thresholds, maximum two test workers. Native Bun acceptance passed all three hold modes. npm run acceptance:migration passed all five real install layouts and 15 captured-artifact hold scenarios, zero remote posts or duplicate receipts; accepted artifact SHA-256 239db9d452c42bf011df1dbed8a932c5758a50ecc3a04b195162c4219fcd7138. The serial full Bun release gate is now running. Existing public-data measurements remain applicable because migration mapping and tracker read paths are unchanged."
  "2026-10-28T23:40:49.296Z",codex-agent,"Re-review full validation complete: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed 968/968 tests, zero failures, all six runtime sources at 100% lines, branches and functions. Both gates ran serially with at most two workers, including unchanged production audit, packaging, changelog and publication-contract checks. No existing tests were weakened or deleted. The sole reported blocking finding is fixed across both shared claim callers and their SDK, CLI and lifecycle-hook paths; no additional actionable non-blocking finding was supplied or present in the reviewed GitHub comments."
  "2026-10-28T23:41:40.670Z",codex-agent,"The registered command pm test pm-slack-destination-migration-plans --run --match destination-drain-routing --progress --timeout 300 passed its selected command, 81/81 assertions/tests, zero failures. PM test-result tracking is disabled by existing policy, so results are retained here without changing that policy. Final pack bytes after both release builds still match accepted SHA-256 239db9d452c42bf011df1dbed8a932c5758a50ecc3a04b195162c4219fcd7138. Ready to push the reviewed fix to PR #169; live CI run links and exact-head counts will be reported in the PR and final report. Item remains open for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-28T23:44:21.195Z",codex-agent,"Final pre-push fetch found origin/main had advanced by Dependabot PR #170 after review work began. Merged d017279 cleanly; it changes only the pm-cli, pm-changelog and pm-ops development pins from 2026.10.24 to 2026.10.25. Reinstalled dependencies with public-registry configuration and no inherited credentials. Reclaimed the item for combined-head validation: rerun focused tests first, then serial full npm and Bun release gates with at most two workers, and recapture the packed artifact because package metadata changed. No tracker history was merged or rewritten."
  "2026-10-29T00:07:50.911Z",codex-agent,"Combined-head validation after merging main is complete: focused destination-drain-routing tests passed 81/81; npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed 968/968, zero failures, 100% lines/branches/functions for all six runtime sources. Gates were serial with at most two workers and unchanged thresholds. Native Bun acceptance passed; npm run acceptance:migration passed five install layouts and 15 captured-artifact hold scenarios with zero remote posts or duplicate receipts. Final accepted artifact SHA-256 is 0b6004f40045884313d93288fa3ca66bfe2b60cf501a11aeb2323b478c42225a (supersedes the pre-merge metadata digest). PM health reports no pending merge receipts. Revert evidence remains valid because merging main changed development pins only. Ready for exact-head CI on PR #169; live run URL and final counts will be included in the PR and final report. Leave this item open for orchestrator verification."
